{"results":[{"url":"https://sansad.in/getFile/lsapps/loksabhaquestions/annex/185/AU57_62NgO2.pdf?source=lsapps","final_url":"https://sansad.in/getFile/lsapps/loksabhaquestions/annex/185/AU57_62NgO2.pdf?source=lsapps","title":null,"description":null,"language":null,"text":"GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 57 \nANSWERED ON 21.07.2025 \n \nCoaching Centers for Preparation of UPSC Examination \n \n57. Shri Adhikari Deepak Dev: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:  \n(a) the number of coaching centers authorised by the Central Government for UPSC exam in the \ncountry; \n(b) the details of coaching centers being run for preparation of UPSC examination, State-wise; and \n(c) the action taken by the Government against unauthorised coaching centers, year-wise? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n(DR. SUKANTA MAJUMDAR) \n \n(a) to (c): Education is in the concurrent list, the State and UT Government need to take proactive \naction on the matter of Coaching Institutes. In order to regulate the Private Coaching and tuition \nclasses, a number of States/UTs have brought out guidelines / regulations / legislations. Majority of \nthese coaching centers spread across the country are commercial entities which need to be regulated \nas per the law of the respective States / UTs. Ministry of Education has also circulated a Guidelines \nfor Regulation of Coaching Center to States/UTs on 16.01.2024. \n \nDepartment of Social Justice and Empowerment, Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment runs \na Scheme namely Free coaching for SCs, OBCs and beneficiaries of PM CARES Children Scheme, \nfor imparting coaching for competitive examinations for obtaining appropriate jobs in \nPublic/Private Sector including Civil Services Examination and/or for securing admission in \nreputed technical and professional higher educational institutions. The Scheme is being \nimplemented by Dr. Ambedkar Foundation through Dr. Ambedkar Centre of Excellence (DACE) \nestablished in empanelled Central Universities. As on date, a total of 19 Central Universities are \nempanelled under the Scheme.  \n \nThe Residential Coaching Academy (RCA) scheme was initiated in 2009 by University Grants \nCommission (UGC) to support students from Minority communities, SC/STs, and women by \nproviding them with equal opportunities through specialized coaching. Launched in select central \nuniversities—Aligarh Muslim University (AMU), Maulana Azad National Urdu University \n(MANUU), Jamia Millia Islamia (JMI), Jamia Hamdard, and Babasaheb Bhimrao Ambedkar \nUniversity—the scheme offers residential coaching for competitive exams, including Central/State \nGovernment services, banking, and private sector jobs. The scheme does not charge tuition fees but \nmay levy nominal registration and hostel charges. \n \nDepartment of Consumer Affairs, the Central Consumer Protection Authority (CCPA) imposes \npenalty on coaching institutes for making misleading advertisements and directs them to \ndiscontinue such advertisements. \n***","author":"DELL","published_date":null,"latency_ms":1874.113434998435,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}